schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "95% of Sarafu users called the network important to their household economy (2025 survey)"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    In Grassroots Economics' 2025 survey of the Sarafu community-currency
    network in Kenya, 95% of users called the network important or very
    important to their household economy.
  evidence: >-
    Cited to "Grassroots Economics, 2025 survey" (grassecon.substack.com/p/
    2025-sarafu-network-study-results) in the article's References.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/why-regens-interested.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's grounded, non-speculative example of "ownership that
    stays local" — money designed to circulate rather than be flipped for
    profit — as a contrast to the article's opening warning about crypto
    speculation and scams.
  uncertainty: >-
    Self-reported network survey conducted/published by Grassroots Economics
    itself (the organization running Sarafu), not an independent third-party
    study; sample size and methodology are not described in this article.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/why-regens-interested.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
